    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d440-a18">

                <pb facs="0414" n="340" sameAs="frus:frus1865p2/pg340"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg></opener>

                <head>Mr. Bigelow to Mr.
                        Charpentier</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Paris,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1865-05-15"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >May</hi> 15, 1865.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your letter dated 10th May, and of the enclosure accompanying it, which I
                    will hasten, in conformity with your desire, to forward to the address you have
                    indicated to me.</p>
                <p>Nothing can be more consoling to my compatriots, in the midst of our national
                    mourning, <pb facs="0415" n="341" xml:id="pg341"/> than to learn how much their
                    sorrow is shared in Europe, and I pray you to become the organ to the lodge “The
                    Friends of Order” in Paris of all my gratitude for the sympathy which it sends
                    to my country and to its government.</p>
                <p>Accept, sir, the assurance of my very distinguished sentiments.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>JOHN BIGELOW.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Charpentier.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
